/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 70 0 R
/T (Over the past few years, educational institutions have gradually shifted toward digital systems for handling student records, access control, and identity verification. Today, stu- dents commonly use digital credentials to access services such as institutional platforms, discounts, and age-restricted facilities. Even though these systems have improved efficiency, the method used for identity verification has not evolved much. In most situations, students are still required to present their complete identity document just to verify a single piece of information, such as age or enrollment status. This results in unnecessary sharing of personal details that are not relevant to the request. Because of this, third-party vendors often end up storing sensitive information, which increases the chances of data misuse or security breaches.)
/E (Over the past few years, educational institutions have gradually shifted toward digital systems for handling student records, access control, and identity verification. Today, stu- dents commonly use digital credentials to access services such as institutional platforms, discounts, and age-restricted facilities. Even though these systems have improved efficiency, the method used for identity verification has not evolved much. In most situations, students are still required to present their complete identity document just to verify a single piece of information, such as age or enrollment status. This results in unnecessary sharing of personal details that are not relevant to the request. Because of this, third-party vendors often end up storing sensitive information, which increases the chances of data misuse or security breaches.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
