/T (In practical implementations, the combination of Spring Boot and Angular has become quite common for building scalable and secure web applications. Spring Boot is widely used for backend services, particularly in systems that follow zero-trust principles, where continuous verification is required. At the same time, Angular provides a responsive and effi- cient frontend framework. Recent work also highlights the role of WebAssembly \(WASM\) in enabling complex cryptographic operations directly within the browser. This makes it possible to perform tasks like Zero-Knowledge Proof generation on the client side, improving both performance and data privacy.)
